#
# Example requests for the IntelliJ HTTP Client (click the green ▶ next to a request).
# Start the API first: mvn spring-boot:run

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Health page
GET {{host}}/health

### Actuator health (technical)
GET {{host}}/actuator/health

### Calculator: 1 + 2
GET {{host}}/api/calculator/add?numbers=1&numbers=2

### Calculator: 1 + 2 + 3 with JSON body
POST {{host}}/api/calculator/calculate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "operation": "ADD",
  "numbers": [1, 2, 3]
}

### Calculator: only one number -> 400 Bad Request
GET {{host}}/api/calculator/add?numbers=5

### Calculator: 5 - 3
GET {{host}}/api/calculator/subtract?numbers=5&numbers=3

### Calculator: 2 * 3 * 4
GET {{host}}/api/calculator/multiply?numbers=2&numbers=3&numbers=4

### Calculator: 12 / 3 / 2
GET {{host}}/api/calculator/divide?numbers=12&numbers=3&numbers=2

### Ticket price: child (10) on a school day -> 1.60
GET {{host}}/api/tickets/price?age=10&dateTime=2026-11-11T10:00:00

### Ticket price: child (10) on a Sunday -> 0
GET {{host}}/api/tickets/price?age=10&dateTime=2026-11-22T10:00:00

### Buy a ticket: adult pays 5.00 -> change 1.80
POST {{host}}/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "age": 30,
  "payment": 5.00,
  "dateTime": "2026-11-11T10:00:00"
}

### Buy a ticket: insufficient payment -> 400 Bad Request
POST {{host}}/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "age": 30,
  "payment": 1.00
}

### School holidays 2026/27
GET {{host}}/api/school-holidays/2026

### Is 28.12.2026 a school holiday?
GET {{host}}/api/school-holidays/check?date=2026-12-28
